# FIX-RME-CONSENT-WORKFLOW-PRINT-UX-2 — durable rules

## 1. Consent is the RME AUTHORING gate

> **SUPERSEDED by FIX-RME-EXAM-CONSENT-ODONTOGRAM-HISTORY-3 (FIX-02 / FIX-03).**
> This section previously read "Consent is the RME payment gate". It is not.
> See `.cursor/rules/109-rme-exam-consent-odontogram-history.mdc` for the
> current workflow; the anti-regression clauses below remain in force.

- A valid signed `PERSETUJUAN TINDAKAN MEDIS` for the current visit is required
  before that visit's **RME may be written** — created, edited, handwritten or
  finalized. It is **not** required to take payment.
- The gate reads **persisted evidence**: `RmeVisitConsentService::hasValidConsent()`
  / `ClinicVisit::hasSignedConsentDocument()`. It must never be satisfied by a
  value carried in any request.
- **Never reintroduce a consent flag that a request supplies.** The original
  defect was `applyConsentVerification()` writing request booleans onto the visit
  and `assertConsentVerified()` reading them back — the gate authored its own
  evidence, so `consent_signed_by_patient=1` paid an invoice. Both of those
  methods are now deleted.
- The UI is not the authority. A disabled button, a hidden card or a Blade
  condition is presentation; `MedicalRecordService` and the handwriting
  controller must fail closed on a crafted POST.
- `consent_signed_by_patient` / `consent_signed_by_doctor` on `trx_clinic_visits`
  are a **display-only historical record** that a paper form was sighted before
  this sprint. They gate nothing, are never written from a request, and are no
  longer read by any authorisation path.

### 1a. Consent is never a payment condition

> **SUPERSEDED.** This section previously said consent was required while the
> visit was at `cashier_pending`. That gate is REMOVED.

- **Payment eligibility is purely financial and workflow-based.** Nothing in
  `RmePaymentService` may consult consent again.
- Consent is consent to TREATMENT, so it belongs where treatment is decided and
  recorded — the doctor's examination — not where money changes hands. A cashier
  is not the right person to adjudicate clinical consent, and a patient at the
  counter is past the point where refusing could change anything.
- The safety property is now STRONGER, not weaker: a treatment that was recorded
  at all already had consent. The old cashier gate only ever fired for a visit
  still at `cashier_pending`, so every carry-over receivable and every instalment
  on an already-completed visit bypassed it by design.
- **Historical receivables must stay collectible.** Every receivable that
  predates the consent architecture has no signed consent. Do not "tighten" this.

### 1b. Consent reads cost queries now

`hasVerifiedConsent()` used to read two casted booleans for free; the signed-document
predicates consult the consent table. **Any list that calls one per row must
eager-load `consents`** — the cashier handoff board is unpaginated by design, so an
N+1 there has no upper bound.

## 2. Consent timing follows the canonical RME flow

> **SUPERSEDED.** The flow below is the current one; consent moved from after
> "Selesai Pemeriksaan" to the start of the examination.

```
Pendaftaran -> Antrian -> Input Ruangan -> Dokter "Mulai Pemeriksaan" (in_progress)
  -> Consent -> RME authoring unlocked -> RME + Odontogram
  -> Dokter "Selesai Pemeriksaan" (cashier_pending) -> Pembayaran -> completed
```

- Consent is signable for any **non-terminal** visit, so the doctor takes it at
  the start of the encounter. On a `completed` / `cancelled` visit it fails
  closed, because that would be back-dating evidence.
- The gate window and the signable window are the SAME window, so a blocked
  write always has an unblocking action available and the gate can never
  deadlock a live visit.
- **Terminal visits are never gated**, so Sprint 59 historical revision keeps
  working and no pre-existing record is locked.
- The doctor still advances only `in_progress -> cashier_pending`, and
  `completed` remains cashier/payment-owned. **Finalizing a record no longer
  advances anything** — see rule 109 / FIX-01.

## 3. Consent identity cannot be borrowed

- A signed consent binds patient + visit + form. A consent for another visit,
  another patient or another branch **never** satisfies payment.
- The treating doctor comes from the visit, never from the request.
- `Saya sendiri` copies the canonical patient identity; typed input cannot
  override `mst_patients`.

## 4. Signed consent is evidence

- **Immutable.** No update path, no hard delete. A mistake is **voided with a
  reason** and re-signed; the voided row is kept.
- The agreed wording is **snapshotted** into the consent. Editing
  `config/rme_consent.php` must never retro-change a signed consent — bump
  `version` when the substance changes.
- The consent clause text is the clinic's printed form. Do not rephrase, extend
  or trim it without a new product decision. Formatting normalisation only.

## 5. Documentation consent (clause 8) is separate and non-coercive

- Must be an **explicit YA/TIDAK**. No default, and a signature is not implied
  agreement to publication.
- Validate as `present|boolean`, never `required` — `required` rejects `0`.
- **Payment eligibility must never depend on answering YA.** A valid consent
  with clause 8 = TIDAK still opens payment.

## 6. Consent permissions

- `manage_rme_consents` (sign/void), `view_rme_consents` (read/print).
- Held by Doctor, Kasir, Admin Klinik, Supervisor RME.
- **Do not gate consent on `manage_clinic_visits`: Kasir does not hold it**, and
  doing so 403s the role that must complete every payment. Consent routes sit
  inside the RME group, which already requires
  `view_clinic_visits|manage_clinic_visits`.
- Audit **effective** permissions (`$user->can()`), never direct rows, and never
  test with Super Admin (`Gate::before` bypasses everything).

## 7. Consent PII

- The consent document is the **only** surface that renders a full identity
  number, because the form legally records "No KTP/SIM". It is permission-gated
  and branch-scoped.
- Identity numbers and signature paths are `$hidden` on the model — never JSON,
  logs or listings.
- Signatures live on a **private disk** with no public URL, and are streamed only
  through the consent policy.

## 8. Medical Record page ownership

- Information hierarchy: **Informasi Kunjungan -> RME Tulisan Tangan ->
  Dokumen RME Pasien**.
- **Finalisasi** and **Cetak RME** belong to the Medical Record page header.
- Moved, not duplicated: exactly one Finalisasi control and one print entry
  point.
- The page's `$clinicVisit` is the **active sheet's** visit
  (`$activeSheet->clinicVisit`). Any per-visit action here must use it, not a
  canonical or source visit, or it acts on a different visit than the one shown.

## 9. Print ownership

- **Cetak RME** lives on the Medical Record page, **not** on Detail Kunjungan.
  This supersedes the FIX-CLINIC-OPS (FIX-07) rule that Admin Klinik's visit
  detail is "read-only plus Cetak RME"; the front office reaches it through a
  **navigation link** to Rekam Medis instead.
- **RME print contains no odontogram.** The odontogram has its own standalone
  print (`rme.odontograms.print`), which is unchanged.
- Removing the odontogram from the print is **composition only** — never delete
  the odontogram model, table, workflow, UI or standalone print.
- Relocating a print button must never create a second print endpoint.

## 10. The kwitansi is one page

- The RME receipt is designed as a **one-page** print/PDF for the supported
  transaction envelope.
- **Financial data must never be clipped, hidden or dropped to force one page.**
  No `overflow:hidden`, no `display:none` on money, no unreadable type, no
  removed rows. Beyond the envelope the document **continues**; it is never
  truncated.
- Every print template must declare an `@page` box. The missing one here was the
  root cause of the second sheet.
- Prove the contract with **real renderer output** — render through dompdf and
  read the page count with poppler `pdfinfo` — and pair it with a content
  assertion, because a page count alone can be satisfied by deleting rows.
- The kwitansi is a *pelunasan* document: both receipt routes are `PAID`-only.

## 11. Testing

- Tests that exercise **payment mechanics** may use `rmeSignedConsentFor($visit)`.
- Tests about **consent itself** (timing, signature, authorisation, branch scope)
  must go through `RmeVisitConsentService` so the rules stay under test.
- A "does not contain" assertion on a PDF is vacuous unless extraction is proven
  to work — always assert something expected is present first.
